IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa27-definitions.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 "Interpretation" and the index of defined
-- expressions: ss 1260 (associate), 1261 (minor definitions, "established in the United Kingdom") and 1262 (index),
-- lines 17938-18044 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
--   JUST TRUE  the text says the case is within the term.
--   JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words ("means", "if and only if", "other than").
--   NOTHING    the text does not decide: "includes" (list not closed), a term handed to another instrument
--              (points outside the text), silent, undefined term, or limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- WHY THIS MODULE REDEFINES KEEL TERMS. Section 1261(1) gives "the competent authority", "firm", "officer",
-- "director" and "company" their meaning "in this Part" (Part 42). The keel's coa-definitions.l4 answers the same
-- words for the whole Act (s 1173(1)); a Part 42 provision uses THESE functions, not the keel's inputs.
-- This module is the base of the part's modules: it imports only the core; the others import it.
-- Every top-level name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1260 Meaning of "associate"
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The four kinds of person the section distinguishes. A partnership is "a legal person" under Scots law and
-- under the law of any other country or territory in which a partnership is a legal person (subsection (4));
-- otherwise it is not (subsection (5)).
DECLARE `s 1260 kind of subject` IS ONE OF
    `s 1260 an individual`
    `s 1260 a body corporate`
    `s 1260 a partnership that is a legal person`
    `s 1260 a partnership that is not a legal person`

-- The facts about the person who may or may not be an associate of the subject (the "candidate"). Each field is a
-- fact a witness can state about the candidate's relationship to the subject; the rules below say which count.
DECLARE `s 1260 candidate` HAS
    `s 1260 is the spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child of the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is a limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 the subject is a director of the candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 the subject is a member of the candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is an employee or partner of the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is a body corporate in the same group as the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is an employee or partner of a body corporate in the same group as the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is an employee of or partner in the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1260 is an associate of a partner in the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17954 | (6) In subsections (2)(b), (3)(a) and (4)(a), in the case of a body corporate which is a limited liability partnership, “director” is to be read as “member”.
@ref s 1260(6) Meaning of associate: limited liability partnership (src:17954-17954)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1260(6) the subject counts as a director of the candidate body corporate` MEANS
    c's `s 1260 is a body corporate`
    AND IF c's `s 1260 is a limited liability partnership`
        THEN c's `s 1260 the subject is a member of the candidate`   -- "director" is to be read as "member"
        ELSE c's `s 1260 the subject is a director of the candidate`

-- src:17941 | (2) In relation to an individual, “associate” means—
-- src:17942 | (a) that individual's spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child,
-- src:17943 | (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and
-- src:17944 | (c) any employee or partner of that individual.
@ref s 1260(2) Meaning of associate: an individual (src:17941-17944)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1260(2) the candidate is an associate of the individual` MEANS
    IF       c's `s 1260 is the spouse, civil partner or minor child or step-child of the subject`
          OR `s 1260(6) the subject counts as a director of the candidate body corporate` c
          OR c's `s 1260 is an employee or partner of the subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to an individual, “associate” means—"

-- src:17945 | (3) In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means—
-- src:17946 | (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director,
-- src:17947 | (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and
-- src:17948 | (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group.
@ref s 1260(3) Meaning of associate: a body corporate (src:17945-17948)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1260(3) the candidate is an associate of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF       `s 1260(6) the subject counts as a director of the candidate body corporate` c
          OR c's `s 1260 is a body corporate in the same group as the subject`
          OR c's `s 1260 is an employee or partner of the subject`
          OR c's `s 1260 is an employee or partner of a body corporate in the same group as the subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means—"

-- src:17949 | (4) In relation to a partnership constituted under the law of Scotland, or any other country or territory in which a partnership is a legal person, “associate” means—
-- src:17950 | (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director,
-- src:17951 | (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and
-- src:17952 | (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership.
@ref s 1260(4) Meaning of associate: a partnership that is a legal person (src:17949-17952)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1260(4) the candidate is an associate of the partnership that is a legal person` MEANS
    IF       `s 1260(6) the subject counts as a director of the candidate body corporate` c
          OR c's `s 1260 is an employee of or partner in the partnership`
          OR c's `s 1260 is an associate of a partner in the partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associate” means—"

-- src:17953 | (5) In relation to a partnership constituted under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or the law of any other country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners.
@ref s 1260(5) Meaning of associate: a partnership that is not a legal person (src:17953-17953)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1260(5) the candidate is an associate of the partnership that is not a legal person` MEANS
    IF c's `s 1260 is an associate of a partner in the partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners"

-- src:17940 | (1) In this Part “associate”, in relation to a person, is to be construed as follows.
@ref s 1260(1) Meaning of associate (src:17940-17940)
GIVEN k IS A `s 1260 kind of subject`
      c IS A `s 1260 candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1260(1) the candidate is an associate of the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `s 1260 an individual` THEN `s 1260(2) the candidate is an associate of the individual` c
    WHEN `s 1260 a body corporate` THEN `s 1260(3) the candidate is an associate of the body corporate` c
    WHEN `s 1260 a partnership that is a legal person` THEN `s 1260(4) the candidate is an associate of the partnership that is a legal person` c
    WHEN `s 1260 a partnership that is not a legal person` THEN `s 1260(5) the candidate is an associate of the partnership that is not a legal person` c

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1261 Minor definitions (subsection (1), "In this Part, unless a contrary intention appears")
-- =========================================================================================================
-- Every definition below is subject to "unless a contrary intention appears". That is a limit in the text's own
-- wording that a witness cannot state as a fact about the case, so it is not threaded through each function; it is
-- recorded once here, and in NOTES.md (fork register), and each function answers for the case where no contrary
-- intention appears.

DECLARE `s 1261(1) meaning of address` IS ONE OF
    `s 1261(1)(a) the individual's usual residential or business address`
    `s 1261(1)(b) the firm's registered or principal office in the United Kingdom`

-- src:17957 | “address” means—
-- src:17958 | (a) in relation to an individual, his usual residential or business address;
-- src:17959 | (b) in relation to a firm, its registered or principal office in the United Kingdom;
@ref s 1261(1) address (src:17957-17959)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A `s 1261(1) meaning of address`
`s 1261(1) the meaning of address for` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `s 1261(1)(a) the individual's usual residential or business address`
    -- a "firm" is any entity that is not an individual (s 1261(1) "firm"), so every other kind of person is a firm
    OTHERWISE `s 1261(1)(b) the firm's registered or principal office in the United Kingdom`

-- src:17961 | “the Audit Regulation ” means Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities;
@ref s 1261(1) the Audit Regulation (src:17961-17961)
GIVEN `the instrument is Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the instrument is the Audit Regulation` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Audit Regulation ” means Regulation 537/2014"

-- src:17963 | “audit working papers and investigation reports” means—
-- src:17964 | (a) any documents which are or have been held by a statutory auditor ... or a third country auditor and which are related to the conduct of an audit conducted by that auditor;
-- src:17965 | (b) any report of an inspection of the conduct of an audit by a statutory auditor ... or a third country auditor, or
-- src:17966 | (c) any report of an investigation into the conduct of a statutory auditor ... or a third country auditor,
@ref s 1261(1) audit working papers and investigation reports (src:17963-17966)
GIVEN `the document is or has been held by a statutory auditor or a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is related to the conduct of an audit conducted by that auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a report of an inspection of the conduct of an audit by a statutory auditor or a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a report of an investigation into the conduct of a statutory auditor or a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the document is within audit working papers and investigation reports` MEANS
    IF       (`the document is or has been held by a statutory auditor or a third country auditor`
              AND `the document is related to the conduct of an audit conducted by that auditor`)
          OR `the document is a report of an inspection of the conduct of an audit by a statutory auditor or a third country auditor`
          OR `the document is a report of an investigation into the conduct of a statutory auditor or a third country auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“audit working papers and investigation reports” means—"

-- src:17967 | “company” means any company or other body the accounts of which must be audited in accordance with Part 16;
@ref s 1261(1) company (src:17967-17967)
GIVEN `the accounts of the body must be audited in accordance with Part 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the body is a company for this Part` MEANS
    IF `the accounts of the body must be audited in accordance with Part 16`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means any company or other body the accounts of which must be audited in accordance with Part 16"

-- src:17968 | “the competent authority” means the Financial Reporting Council Limited
@ref s 1261(1) the competent authority (src:17968-17968)
GIVEN `the body is the Financial Reporting Council Limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the body is the competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Financial Reporting Council Limited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the competent authority” means the Financial Reporting Council Limited"

-- src:17969 | “the data protection legislation” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
@ref s 1261(1) the data protection legislation (src:17969-17969)
-- The meaning is handed to section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018, which is not among the sources: the borrowed
-- answer is an input, and NOTHING passes through as NOTHING.
GIVEN `the legislation is the data protection legislation within the meaning of section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the legislation is the data protection legislation` MEANS
    `the legislation is the data protection legislation within the meaning of section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING

-- src:17970 | “director”, in relation to a body corporate, includes any person occupying in relation to it the position of a director (by whatever name called) and any person in accordance with whose directions or instructions (not being advice given in a professional capacity) the directors of the body are accustomed to act;
@ref s 1261(1) director (src:17970-17970)
GIVEN `the person is a director in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person occupies in relation to the body corporate the position of a director (by whatever name called)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the body are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those directions or instructions are advice given in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the person is a director of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a director in the ordinary sense`
          OR `the person occupies in relation to the body corporate the position of a director (by whatever name called)`
          OR (       `the directors of the body are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions`
               AND (NOT `those directions or instructions are advice given in a professional capacity`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“director”, in relation to a body corporate, includes"

-- src:17973 | “firm” means any entity, whether or not a legal person, which is not an individual and includes a body corporate, a corporation sole and a partnership or other unincorporated association;
@ref s 1261(1) firm (src:17973-17973)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the entity is a firm` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“firm” means any entity, whether or not a legal person, which is not an individual"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- a body corporate, a corporation sole, a partnership or other unincorporated association: all named by "includes"

-- Kleene "or" over two borrowed answers, so that NOTHING (points outside the text) is never read as FALSE.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) group: either answer holds` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            IF y THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:17974 | “group”, in relation to a body corporate, means the body corporate, any other body corporate which is its holding company or subsidiary and any other body corporate which is a subsidiary of that holding company;
-- src:17975 | “holding company” and “subsidiary” are to be read in accordance with section 1159 and Schedule 6;
@ref s 1261(1) group, holding company and subsidiary (src:17974-17975)
-- "holding company" and "subsidiary" are read in accordance with section 1159 and Schedule 6: the keel answers the
-- first (s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company) and Schedule 6 is part coa29's, so each is a
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN input.
GIVEN `the other body corporate is the body corporate itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other body corporate is a holding company of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other body corporate is a subsidiary of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other body corporate is a subsidiary of a holding company of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the other body corporate is in the same group as the body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the other body corporate is the body corporate itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `s 1261(1) group: either answer holds`
                    (`s 1261(1) group: either answer holds`
                        `the other body corporate is a holding company of the body corporate`
                        `the other body corporate is a subsidiary of the body corporate`)
                    `the other body corporate is a subsidiary of a holding company of the body corporate`
        WHEN JUST g THEN
            IF g THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“group”, in relation to a body corporate, means"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): holding company and subsidiary are read under s 1159 and Schedule 6

GIVEN `section 1159 and Schedule 6 answer that the company is a holding company or subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the company is a holding company or subsidiary as sections 1159 and Schedule 6 read` MEANS
    `section 1159 and Schedule 6 answer that the company is a holding company or subsidiary`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING

-- src:17976 | “officer”, in relation to a body corporate, includes a director, a manager, a secretary or, where the affairs of the body are managed by its members, a member;
@ref s 1261(1) officer (src:17976-17976)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a manager of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a secretary of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affairs of the body are managed by its members and the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the person is an officer of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a director of the body corporate`
          OR `the person is a manager of the body corporate`
          OR `the person is a secretary of the body corporate`
          OR `the affairs of the body are managed by its members and the person is a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer”, in relation to a body corporate, includes"

-- src:17977 | “parent undertaking” and “subsidiary undertaking” are to be read in accordance with section 1162 and Schedule 7.
@ref s 1261(1) parent undertaking and subsidiary undertaking (src:17977-17977)
GIVEN `section 1162 and Schedule 7 answer that the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking as section 1162 and Schedule 7 read` MEANS
    `section 1162 and Schedule 7 answer that the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING

-- src:17978 | “regulated market” has the meaning given in Article 2(1)(13) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012;
@ref s 1261(1) regulated market (src:17978-17978)
GIVEN `Article 2(1)(13) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 answers that the market is a regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the market is a regulated market` MEANS
    `Article 2(1)(13) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 answers that the market is a regulated market`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING

-- src:17979 | “third country” means a country or territory other than the United Kingdom;
@ref s 1261(1) third country (src:17979-17979)
GIVEN `the country or territory is the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the country or territory is a third country` MEANS
    IF `the country or territory is the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“third country” means a country or territory other than the United Kingdom"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:17980 | “ third country auditor ” means a person, other than ... a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, who is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate incorporated or formed under the law of a third country in accordance with the law of that country;
@ref s 1261(1) third country auditor (src:17980-17980)
GIVEN `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate incorporated or formed under the law of a third country in accordance with the law of that country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the person is a third country auditor` MEANS
    IF       (NOT `the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`)
         AND `the person is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate incorporated or formed under the law of a third country in accordance with the law of that country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ third country auditor ” means a person, other than ... a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor"

-- src:17981 | “third country competent authority” means a body established in a third country exercising functions related to the regulation or oversight of auditors;
@ref s 1261(1) third country competent authority (src:17981-17981)
GIVEN `the body is established in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body exercises functions related to the regulation or oversight of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the body is a third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is established in a third country` AND `the body exercises functions related to the regulation or oversight of auditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“third country competent authority” means a body established in a third country exercising functions related to the regulation or oversight of auditors"

-- src:17982 | “transfer”, in relation to audit working papers and investigation reports, includes physical and electronic transfer and allowing access to such papers;
@ref s 1261(1) transfer (src:17982-17982)
GIVEN `the act is a physical transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is an electronic transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is allowing access to the papers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1261(1) the act is a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports` MEANS
    IF `the act is a physical transfer` OR `the act is an electronic transfer` OR `the act is allowing access to the papers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“transfer”, in relation to audit working papers and investigation reports, includes"

